<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Unterland (Liechtenstein)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Liechtenstein Unterland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Unterland is the northern of the two traditional regions of Liechtenstein, corresponding to the former Lordship of Schellenberg. It comprises the five municipalities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eschen">Eschen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamprin">Gamprin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauren">Mauren</a>, Ruggell and Schellenberg and forms one of the country's two electoral districts. The Oberland, the former County of Vaduz, makes up the rest of the principality.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/unterland-liechtenstein.jpg" alt="Unterland (Liechtenstein)" width="320" height="628" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willtron · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liechtenstein-Unterland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
